{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The workspace is what the agent boots into: a cloned, installed repo with the\ncommands you want it to run. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineWorkspace()"},{"type":"text","value":" describes that working tree\nonce. Each harness adapter projects it into its own native format,\nand it runs inside whichever "},{"type":"link","href":"./providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider"}]},{"type":"text","value":" you chose. This page covers\nthe working tree itself: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packageManager"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scripts"},{"type":"text","value":".\nSecrets, skills, and MCP servers live on "},{"type":"link","href":"./provisioning","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provisioning"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  // Where the working tree comes from.\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }),\n  // Package manager (auto-detected from the lockfile when omitted).\n  packageManager: 'pnpm',\n  // Commands run once during bootstrap.\n  setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n  // Named commands the agent can run.\n  scripts: { test: 'pnpm test', build: 'pnpm build' },\n  // Injected into the sandbox env at create/resume, never persisted.\n  secrets: createSecrets({ XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '' }),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The fields:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it sets"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where the working tree comes from (git repo, local path, or nothing)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packageManager"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"npm"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"yarn"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bun"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auto"},{"type":"text","value":". Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auto"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commands run once during bootstrap (serial array or serial/parallel groups)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scripts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Named commands the agent and user can invoke by name."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"secrets"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed secret refs injected into the env. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./provisioning","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provisioning"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineWorkspace()"},{"type":"text","value":" also takes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructions"},{"type":"text","value":" for\nprovisioning the agent environment. Those are covered on\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./provisioning","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provisioning"}]},{"type":"text","value":" rather than duplicated here."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"source","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":" is where the working tree comes from. Five shapes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineWorkspace, githubRepo, gitSource } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\n// Shorthand for a GitHub repo (owner/repo or a full URL).\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }) })\n\n// Any git URL.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: gitSource({ url: 'https://git.example.com/owner/repo.git' }) })\n\n// The same as gitSource, written out as a plain object.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'git', url: 'https://github.com/owner/repo', ref: 'main' } })\n\n// An existing directory on the host (e.g. local-process dev loop).\ndefineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'local', path: '/abs/path/to/repo' } })\n\n// No working tree: the agent starts in an empty workspace.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"githubRepo"},{"type":"text","value":" is a convenience wrapper over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSource"},{"type":"text","value":": a short "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"owner/repo"},{"type":"text","value":"\nexpands to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"https://github.com/owner/repo.git"},{"type":"text","value":", while a full URL is used as-is.\nBoth produce a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'git' }"},{"type":"text","value":" source, so you can also write that object\nliteral directly when you want full control."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"shallow-clone-by-default","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shallow clone by default"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"githubRepo"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSource"},{"type":"text","value":" default to a shallow single-branch clone\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--depth 1 --single-branch"},{"type":"text","value":") so cold starts stay fast. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"depth"},{"type":"text","value":" number\nfor a specific history depth, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'full'"},{"type":"text","value":" to fetch everything:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\n// Shallow clone (depth 1) is the default.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }) })\n\n// Explicit depth: fetches the last 10 commits.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app', depth: 10 }) })\n\n// Full history: disables the depth flag entirely.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app', depth: 'full' }) })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"package-manager","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package manager"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packageManager"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'npm'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'pnpm'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'yarn'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'bun'"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'auto'"},{"type":"text","value":". It\ndefaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'auto'"},{"type":"text","value":", which detects the manager from the lockfile after the\nsource lands. Set it explicitly when you want to pin the choice rather than\ninfer it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":" runs once during bootstrap to turn a freshly cloned repo into an\ninstalled one. It accepts either a plain string array (every step runs serially) or\na builder callback that records serial and parallel groups."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The simplest form is the array, equivalent to all-serial:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The callback runs over a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"persistent shell"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the working directory and\nenvironment carry over between steps, so a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cd"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"export"},{"type":"text","value":" in a serial step is\nvisible to the next one. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parallel([...])"},{"type":"text","value":" to launch independent commands\nconcurrently. They inherit the shell's cwd and env, and the next serial step\nwaits for all of them to finish:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  setup: ({ serial, parallel }) => {\n    // Runs in order on the persistent shell; cwd/env carry over.\n    serial('corepack enable')\n    serial('pnpm install')\n    // Both commands launch concurrently, inheriting cwd + env from the shell.\n    parallel(['pnpm build', 'pnpm typecheck'])\n    // Runs after both parallel steps complete.\n    serial('echo bootstrap done')\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the provider supports snapshots, bootstrap caches the result after\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":" so subsequent runs skip it. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle &amp; snapshots"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"installing-an-agent-cli","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installing an agent CLI"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every step runs through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sh -c"},{"type":"text","value":", and a step fails the bootstrap when its exit\ncode is non-zero. When a step installs a harness CLI globally, make it verify the\nCLI before it returns. The agent CLIs ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@openai/codex"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@anthropic-ai/claude-code"},{"type":"text","value":", …) ship their native binary as a platform-specific\n"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"optional"}]},{"type":"text","value":" dependency, and npm treats optional dependencies as best-effort: a\nfailed download is not an install error, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"npm install -g"},{"type":"text","value":" exits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" and leaves\na CLI that dies later with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Missing optional dependency"},{"type":"text","value":". Running the CLI turns\nthat into a loud bootstrap failure instead of a broken run:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst install = 'npm install -g @openai/codex --include=optional && codex --version'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  // Retry once: the failure above is usually a transient download.\n  setup: [`${install} || { ${install} ; }`],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep each command self-contained. Do not build a step by splicing one command\ninto another ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"`${cmd} || sudo ${cmd}`"},{"type":"text","value":"): a command that starts with a\nsubshell (like the Grok CLI installer, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(curl … || curl …) | bash"},{"type":"text","value":") is not a\nvalid argument to another command, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sh"},{"type":"text","value":" then fails at parse time with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"syntax error: unexpected \"(\""},{"type":"text","value":" (exit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2"},{"type":"text","value":") without running anything."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some providers run as a non-root user. Workspace-local installs such as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm install"},{"type":"text","value":" do not need sudo. System or global package installs on those\nproviders need non-interactive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sudo -n"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":". See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"./policy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Policy"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"scripts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scripts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scripts"},{"type":"text","value":" is a map of named commands the agent and user can invoke by name,\nwithout restating the full command line each time:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  scripts: {\n    test: 'pnpm test',\n    build: 'pnpm build',\n    typecheck: 'pnpm test:types',\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are surfaced as named commands rather than freeform shell, which also\ngives "},{"type":"link","href":"./policy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Policy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a stable name to allow, ask about, or deny."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"source","text":"Source","level":2},{"id":"shallow-clone-by-default","text":"Shallow clone by default","level":3},{"id":"package-manager","text":"Package manager","level":2},{"id":"setup","text":"Setup","level":2},{"id":"installing-an-agent-cli","text":"Installing an agent CLI","level":3},{"id":"scripts","text":"Scripts","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe workspace is what the agent boots into: a cloned, installed repo with the\ncommands you want it to run. `defineWorkspace()` describes that working tree\nonce. Each harness adapter projects it into its own native format,\nand it runs inside whichever [provider](./providers) you chose. This page covers\nthe working tree itself: `source`, `packageManager`, `setup`, and `scripts`.\nSecrets, skills, and MCP servers live on [Provisioning](./provisioning).\n\n```ts\nimport { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  // Where the working tree comes from.\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }),\n  // Package manager (auto-detected from the lockfile when omitted).\n  packageManager: 'pnpm',\n  // Commands run once during bootstrap.\n  setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n  // Named commands the agent can run.\n  scripts: { test: 'pnpm test', build: 'pnpm build' },\n  // Injected into the sandbox env at create/resume, never persisted.\n  secrets: createSecrets({ XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '' }),\n})\n```\n\nThe fields:\n\n| Field            | What it sets                                                              |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source`         | Where the working tree comes from (git repo, local path, or nothing).     |\n| `packageManager` | `npm` / `pnpm` / `yarn` / `bun` / `auto`. Defaults to `auto`.              |\n| `setup`          | Commands run once during bootstrap (serial array or serial/parallel groups). |\n| `scripts`        | Named commands the agent and user can invoke by name.                     |\n| `secrets`        | Typed secret refs injected into the env. See [Provisioning](./provisioning). |\n\n> `defineWorkspace()` also takes `skills`, `plugins`, and `instructions` for\n> provisioning the agent environment. Those are covered on\n> [Provisioning](./provisioning) rather than duplicated here.\n\n## Source\n\n`source` is where the working tree comes from. Five shapes:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo, gitSource } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\n// Shorthand for a GitHub repo (owner/repo or a full URL).\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }) })\n\n// Any git URL.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: gitSource({ url: 'https://git.example.com/owner/repo.git' }) })\n\n// The same as gitSource, written out as a plain object.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'git', url: 'https://github.com/owner/repo', ref: 'main' } })\n\n// An existing directory on the host (e.g. local-process dev loop).\ndefineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'local', path: '/abs/path/to/repo' } })\n\n// No working tree: the agent starts in an empty workspace.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } })\n```\n\n`githubRepo` is a convenience wrapper over `gitSource`: a short `owner/repo`\nexpands to `https://github.com/owner/repo.git`, while a full URL is used as-is.\nBoth produce a `{ type: 'git' }` source, so you can also write that object\nliteral directly when you want full control.\n\n### Shallow clone by default\n\n`githubRepo` and `gitSource` default to a shallow single-branch clone\n(`--depth 1 --single-branch`) so cold starts stay fast. Pass a `depth` number\nfor a specific history depth, or `'full'` to fetch everything:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\n// Shallow clone (depth 1) is the default.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }) })\n\n// Explicit depth: fetches the last 10 commits.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app', depth: 10 }) })\n\n// Full history: disables the depth flag entirely.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app', depth: 'full' }) })\n```\n\n## Package manager\n\n`packageManager` is `'npm'`, `'pnpm'`, `'yarn'`, `'bun'`, or `'auto'`. It\ndefaults to `'auto'`, which detects the manager from the lockfile after the\nsource lands. Set it explicitly when you want to pin the choice rather than\ninfer it.\n\n## Setup\n\n`setup` runs once during bootstrap to turn a freshly cloned repo into an\ninstalled one. It accepts either a plain string array (every step runs serially) or\na builder callback that records serial and parallel groups.\n\nThe simplest form is the array, equivalent to all-serial:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n})\n```\n\nThe callback runs over a **persistent shell**: the working directory and\nenvironment carry over between steps, so a `cd` or `export` in a serial step is\nvisible to the next one. Use `parallel([...])` to launch independent commands\nconcurrently. They inherit the shell's cwd and env, and the next serial step\nwaits for all of them to finish:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  setup: ({ serial, parallel }) => {\n    // Runs in order on the persistent shell; cwd/env carry over.\n    serial('corepack enable')\n    serial('pnpm install')\n    // Both commands launch concurrently, inheriting cwd + env from the shell.\n    parallel(['pnpm build', 'pnpm typecheck'])\n    // Runs after both parallel steps complete.\n    serial('echo bootstrap done')\n  },\n})\n```\n\n> When the provider supports snapshots, bootstrap caches the result after\n> `setup` so subsequent runs skip it. See\n> [Lifecycle &amp; snapshots](./lifecycle).\n\n### Installing an agent CLI\n\nEvery step runs through `sh -c`, and a step fails the bootstrap when its exit\ncode is non-zero. When a step installs a harness CLI globally, make it verify the\nCLI before it returns. The agent CLIs (`@openai/codex`,\n`@anthropic-ai/claude-code`, …) ship their native binary as a platform-specific\n**optional** dependency, and npm treats optional dependencies as best-effort: a\nfailed download is not an install error, so `npm install -g` exits `0` and leaves\na CLI that dies later with `Missing optional dependency`. Running the CLI turns\nthat into a loud bootstrap failure instead of a broken run:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst install = 'npm install -g @openai/codex --include=optional && codex --version'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  // Retry once: the failure above is usually a transient download.\n  setup: [`${install} || { ${install} ; }`],\n})\n```\n\nKeep each command self-contained. Do not build a step by splicing one command\ninto another (`` `${cmd} || sudo ${cmd}` ``): a command that starts with a\nsubshell (like the Grok CLI installer, `(curl … || curl …) | bash`) is not a\nvalid argument to another command, and `sh` then fails at parse time with\n`syntax error: unexpected \"(\"` (exit `2`) without running anything.\n\nSome providers run as a non-root user. Workspace-local installs such as\n`pnpm install` do not need sudo. System or global package installs on those\nproviders need non-interactive `sudo -n` in `setup`. See\n[Providers](./providers) and [Policy](./policy).\n\n## Scripts\n\n`scripts` is a map of named commands the agent and user can invoke by name,\nwithout restating the full command line each time:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  scripts: {\n    test: 'pnpm test',\n    build: 'pnpm build',\n    typecheck: 'pnpm test:types',\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThese are surfaced as named commands rather than freeform shell, which also\ngives [Policy](./policy) a stable name to allow, ask about, or deny.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Workspace\nid: workspace\norder: 4\ndescription: \"Describe what the agent sees inside the sandbox: source repo, package manager, setup commands, and named scripts, in one portable definition.\"\n---\n\nThe workspace is what the agent boots into: a cloned, installed repo with the\ncommands you want it to run. `defineWorkspace()` describes that working tree\nonce. Each harness adapter projects it into its own native format,\nand it runs inside whichever [provider](./providers) you chose. This page covers\nthe working tree itself: `source`, `packageManager`, `setup`, and `scripts`.\nSecrets, skills, and MCP servers live on [Provisioning](./provisioning).\n\n```ts\nimport { createSecrets, defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  // Where the working tree comes from.\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }),\n  // Package manager (auto-detected from the lockfile when omitted).\n  packageManager: 'pnpm',\n  // Commands run once during bootstrap.\n  setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n  // Named commands the agent can run.\n  scripts: { test: 'pnpm test', build: 'pnpm build' },\n  // Injected into the sandbox env at create/resume, never persisted.\n  secrets: createSecrets({ XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '' }),\n})\n```\n\nThe fields:\n\n| Field            | What it sets                                                              |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source`         | Where the working tree comes from (git repo, local path, or nothing).     |\n| `packageManager` | `npm` / `pnpm` / `yarn` / `bun` / `auto`. Defaults to `auto`.              |\n| `setup`          | Commands run once during bootstrap (serial array or serial/parallel groups). |\n| `scripts`        | Named commands the agent and user can invoke by name.                     |\n| `secrets`        | Typed secret refs injected into the env. See [Provisioning](./provisioning). |\n\n> `defineWorkspace()` also takes `skills`, `plugins`, and `instructions` for\n> provisioning the agent environment. Those are covered on\n> [Provisioning](./provisioning) rather than duplicated here.\n\n## Source\n\n`source` is where the working tree comes from. Five shapes:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo, gitSource } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\n// Shorthand for a GitHub repo (owner/repo or a full URL).\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/repo', ref: 'main' }) })\n\n// Any git URL.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: gitSource({ url: 'https://git.example.com/owner/repo.git' }) })\n\n// The same as gitSource, written out as a plain object.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'git', url: 'https://github.com/owner/repo', ref: 'main' } })\n\n// An existing directory on the host (e.g. local-process dev loop).\ndefineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'local', path: '/abs/path/to/repo' } })\n\n// No working tree: the agent starts in an empty workspace.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } })\n```\n\n`githubRepo` is a convenience wrapper over `gitSource`: a short `owner/repo`\nexpands to `https://github.com/owner/repo.git`, while a full URL is used as-is.\nBoth produce a `{ type: 'git' }` source, so you can also write that object\nliteral directly when you want full control.\n\n### Shallow clone by default\n\n`githubRepo` and `gitSource` default to a shallow single-branch clone\n(`--depth 1 --single-branch`) so cold starts stay fast. Pass a `depth` number\nfor a specific history depth, or `'full'` to fetch everything:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\n// Shallow clone (depth 1) is the default.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }) })\n\n// Explicit depth: fetches the last 10 commits.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app', depth: 10 }) })\n\n// Full history: disables the depth flag entirely.\ndefineWorkspace({ source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app', depth: 'full' }) })\n```\n\n## Package manager\n\n`packageManager` is `'npm'`, `'pnpm'`, `'yarn'`, `'bun'`, or `'auto'`. It\ndefaults to `'auto'`, which detects the manager from the lockfile after the\nsource lands. Set it explicitly when you want to pin the choice rather than\ninfer it.\n\n## Setup\n\n`setup` runs once during bootstrap to turn a freshly cloned repo into an\ninstalled one. It accepts either a plain string array (every step runs serially) or\na builder callback that records serial and parallel groups.\n\nThe simplest form is the array, equivalent to all-serial:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n})\n```\n\nThe callback runs over a **persistent shell**: the working directory and\nenvironment carry over between steps, so a `cd` or `export` in a serial step is\nvisible to the next one. Use `parallel([...])` to launch independent commands\nconcurrently. They inherit the shell's cwd and env, and the next serial step\nwaits for all of them to finish:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  setup: ({ serial, parallel }) => {\n    // Runs in order on the persistent shell; cwd/env carry over.\n    serial('corepack enable')\n    serial('pnpm install')\n    // Both commands launch concurrently, inheriting cwd + env from the shell.\n    parallel(['pnpm build', 'pnpm typecheck'])\n    // Runs after both parallel steps complete.\n    serial('echo bootstrap done')\n  },\n})\n```\n\n> When the provider supports snapshots, bootstrap caches the result after\n> `setup` so subsequent runs skip it. See\n> [Lifecycle &amp; snapshots](./lifecycle).\n\n### Installing an agent CLI\n\nEvery step runs through `sh -c`, and a step fails the bootstrap when its exit\ncode is non-zero. When a step installs a harness CLI globally, make it verify the\nCLI before it returns. The agent CLIs (`@openai/codex`,\n`@anthropic-ai/claude-code`, …) ship their native binary as a platform-specific\n**optional** dependency, and npm treats optional dependencies as best-effort: a\nfailed download is not an install error, so `npm install -g` exits `0` and leaves\na CLI that dies later with `Missing optional dependency`. Running the CLI turns\nthat into a loud bootstrap failure instead of a broken run:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst install = 'npm install -g @openai/codex --include=optional && codex --version'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  // Retry once: the failure above is usually a transient download.\n  setup: [`${install} || { ${install} ; }`],\n})\n```\n\nKeep each command self-contained. Do not build a step by splicing one command\ninto another (`` `${cmd} || sudo ${cmd}` ``): a command that starts with a\nsubshell (like the Grok CLI installer, `(curl … || curl …) | bash`) is not a\nvalid argument to another command, and `sh` then fails at parse time with\n`syntax error: unexpected \"(\"` (exit `2`) without running anything.\n\nSome providers run as a non-root user. Workspace-local installs such as\n`pnpm install` do not need sudo. System or global package installs on those\nproviders need non-interactive `sudo -n` in `setup`. See\n[Providers](./providers) and [Policy](./policy).\n\n## Scripts\n\n`scripts` is a map of named commands the agent and user can invoke by name,\nwithout restating the full command line each time:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkspace, githubRepo } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\ndefineWorkspace({\n  source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n  scripts: {\n    test: 'pnpm test',\n    build: 'pnpm build',\n    typecheck: 'pnpm test:types',\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThese are surfaced as named commands rather than freeform shell, which also\ngives [Policy](./policy) a stable name to allow, ask about, or deny.\n"}
